cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "XMH: Explainable Metaheuristics via Exact-Coalition Operator-Level Shapley Value Attribution"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Parra Ortiz"
    given-names: "Francisco"
    email: francisco.parra.o@usach.cl
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics Engineering, Universidad de Santiago de Chile (USACH)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0435-1854"
repository-code: "https://github.com/franciscoparrao/xmh"
abstract: >-
  XMH is a Python framework that computes exact Shapley values
  for operator-level attribution in metaheuristic algorithms. The
  framework exploits the observation that metaheuristics use few
  operators (n ∈ {2,3,4}), making exhaustive evaluation of all 2^n
  ≤ 16 coalitions computationally tractable. Instrumented
  implementations are provided for DE, GA, PSO, CMA-ES, SHADE,
  and JADE, together with QuickSHAP, KernelSHAP (canonical
  drop-one-column reformulation) and tracking-based attribution
  baselines.
keywords:
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - Shapley values
  - cooperative game theory
  - metaheuristics
  - evolutionary computation
  - algorithm interpretability
  - operator attribution
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22731835"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
